;; spec:   §3.3 (types §6.5)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 0
;; audit:  clean
;; A named (fn go ..) that is the last step of a `do` whose value is
;; called: the literal's own occurrence reaches the head of a call
;; through a closure value, a use of kind (d), so it is escaping and a
;; heap closure. Its self call (go 0) is a use of kind (a) and says
;; nothing about where the literal went; the checker once let that
;; self call stand for all the literal's uses, classified it a stack
;; closure and never ended its scope. Found by the rule-5 generator
;; (fibgen seed 100149, size 6), minimised by hand.
(defun main () -> i64
  ((do (fn go (k: i64) (if (<= k 0) 0 (go 0)))) 1))
